                'category'=> 'Immigration',
                'content' => '<p>Renewing your OCI (Overseas Citizen of India) card is a mandatory requirement when you renew your foreign passport. This guide walks you through the complete process.</p><h2>Who Needs to Renew?</h2><p>Every OCI cardholder must renew their OCI card when they get a new passport up to the age of 20, and once after turning 50.</p><h2>Documents Required</h2><ul><li>Current valid foreign passport</li><li>Old OCI card</li><li>Old Indian passport (if any)</li><li>Two passport-size photographs</li></ul><h2>Process Overview</h2><ol><li>Apply online at the OCI portal</li><li>Pay the applicable fee</li><li>Submit documents at VFS/Consulate</li><li>Receive OCI card by post (4–8 weeks)</li></ol><h2>Timeline &amp; Costs</h2><p>Standard processing takes 4–8 weeks. Fees vary by country. Contact Services2NRI for a complete quote and assistance.</p>',
