                'slug'    => 'nri-property-management-tips',
                'title'   => '5 Things Every NRI Should Know Before Renting Their India Property',
                'excerpt' => 'Avoid common mistakes NRIs make when renting their India property. Expert advice from our property management team.',
                'category'=> 'Property',
                'content' => '<p>Owning property in India while living abroad presents unique challenges. Here are five critical things every NRI should know before renting out their property.</p><h2>1. Use a Registered Rent Agreement</h2><p>A registered rent agreement is legally binding and protects both parties. Unregistered agreements are not admissible in court.</p><h2>2. Verify Tenant Documents Thoroughly</h2><p>Always verify ID proof, address proof, employment details, and references before finalising a tenant.</p><h2>3. Understand TDS on Rent</h2><p>If annual rent exceeds ₹2.4 lakhs, the tenant must deduct TDS at 31.2% and deposit it with the income tax department. Ensure compliance.</p><h2>4. Hire a Professional Property Manager</h2><p>A local property manager handles tenant issues, maintenance, rent collection, and legal matters on your behalf.</p><h2>5. Maintain Proper Records</h2><p>Keep all rental agreements, payment receipts, and communication records for income tax filing and legal protection.</p>',
