                'title'   => 'NRI Income Tax Return (ITR) Filing Guide',
                'excerpt' => 'A clear guide to filing ITR as an NRI — what income is taxable, deadlines, and how to avoid penalties.',
                'category'=> 'Taxation',
                'content' => '<p>Filing Income Tax Returns (ITR) in India is mandatory for NRIs if their income from Indian sources exceeds ₹2.5 lakhs in a financial year.</p><h2>What Income is Taxable?</h2><ul><li>Rental income from Indian property</li><li>Capital gains from sale of Indian assets</li><li>Interest from NRO accounts</li><li>Income from Indian business or profession</li></ul><h2>Important Deadlines</h2><p>The ITR filing deadline for NRIs is typically July 31st for the previous financial year (April to March).</p><h2>Forms to Use</h2><p>NRIs generally use ITR-2 (no business income) or ITR-3 (with business income).</p><h2>DTAA Benefits</h2><p>India has Double Tax Avoidance Agreements (DTAA) with 90+ countries. You may be eligible to avoid paying tax twice on the same income.</p><p>Services2NRI provides complete ITR filing assistance for NRIs — from document collection to submission.</p>',
